  <prompt>
    Delete the `mammoth` fallback branch in `ComposeEditor.tsx` (`:1667`/`:1718`) and the `docxToTipTapHtml`
    function in `docxBridge.ts`, now that upload (010), browse (011), and open-in-Compose (012) all hydrate a
    server projection. GREP-PROVE zero `mammoth` / `docxToTipTapHtml` call sites remain under
    `Spaarke.Compose.Components`. This is FR-04 and completes F-2 (single auditable reader). CRITICAL: `mammoth`
    STAYS a repo dependency — SprkChat and Notepad still use it — so remove ONLY the Compose usage; do NOT
    uninstall the package.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (Compose client). Expert in the editor mount path and the `docxBridge.ts` client reader. Meticulous about grep-proving deletions and not breaking unrelated `mammoth` consumers. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    The `mammoth` fallback branch and `docxToTipTapHtml` are deleted from the Compose path; a grep under
    `Spaarke.Compose.Components` finds zero `mammoth` / `docxToTipTapHtml` references; `mammoth` remains installed
    for SprkChat/Notepad; the Compose client builds and all three entry paths render via the projection.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      After 010/011/012, every Compose entry path hydrates a server projection, so the editor mount's
      `else { mammoth }` branch (`ComposeEditor.tsx:1667`/`:1718`) is unreachable and the client reader
      `docxToTipTapHtml` (`docxBridge.ts`) is dead for Compose. F-2 requires exactly ONE docx→editor reader — this
      task removes the second one. `mammoth` is a shared repo dependency (SprkChat + Notepad consume it), so only
      the Compose call sites are removed; the package stays. Spec FR-04; design §4 WS-1. Line numbers indicative —
      RE-GREP before deleting.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — delete the `else { mammoth }` fallback branch (`:1667`/`:1718`)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/**/docxBridge.ts — delete `docxToTipTapHtml` (and any now-orphaned `mammoth` import in the Compose path)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/** (SprkChat/Notepad) — OTHER `mammoth` consumers that MUST keep working; do NOT touch</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">Open-in-Compose transient drafts projected server-side — the last of the three entry paths; only after it does the `mammoth` branch become unreachable.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-04">After this task, a grep for `mammoth` / `docxToTipTapHtml` under `Spaarke.Compose.Components` MUST return zero matches. Scope: capture the grep output as PR evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / F-2">Exactly one docx→editor reader (the server projection) may remain for Compose; no second client-side docx parser. Scope: the deletion is what makes F-2 true — do not leave a dormant branch behind.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / dependency retention">`mammoth` MUST remain a repo dependency; SprkChat + Notepad still use it. Scope: do NOT run `npm uninstall mammoth` or remove it from `package.json`; remove ONLY Compose call sites/imports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / BFF Hygiene §10">Client-only task, but still run `/conflict-check` before the PR (`Spaarke.Compose.Components/` overlaps sibling compose worktrees); no BFF publish-size change expected. Scope: state the change scope in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">The editor surface MUST remain theme-correct after the deletion (dark + light). Scope: the projection branch renders correctly in both themes — verified in the ui-tests section.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Grep-proven client-reader deletion; shared-dependency retention; single-reader invariant (F-2)</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/design.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Mount projection branch (survivor)" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx:1667">
        `if (projection) { server projection } else { mammoth }` — delete the `else` branch; the `if` branch is now the only reader.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Grep-proof deletion" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/">
        `grep -rn "mammoth\|docxToTipTapHtml" src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/` MUST return nothing after deletion.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load spec FR-04, design §4 WS-1, ADR-021 (dark-mode).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep the Compose mammoth surface">Grep `Spaarke.Compose.Components` for `mammoth` and `docxToTipTapHtml`. Confirm the ONLY call sites are the two known branches (`ComposeEditor.tsx:1667`/`:1718`) + `docxToTipTapHtml` in `docxBridge.ts`. If an UNEXPECTED consumer appears, escalate (see escalation).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Delete the fallback + reader">Delete the `else { mammoth }` branch in `ComposeEditor.tsx` and `docxToTipTapHtml` in `docxBridge.ts`; remove now-orphaned `mammoth` imports in the Compose path ONLY. Do NOT touch SprkChat/Notepad or `package.json`.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Grep-prove zero Compose call sites">Re-run the grep; confirm zero `mammoth` / `docxToTipTapHtml` matches under `Spaarke.Compose.Components`. Confirm `mammoth` still resolves for SprkChat/Notepad (grep those still match). Capture output for the PR.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Build + ui-tests + conflict-check">Build the Compose client; run the ui-tests below (projection render, no console errors, ADR-021 dark-mode). Run `/conflict-check`. State the change scope + grep evidence in the PR.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Set task ✅ in tasks/TASK-INDEX.md">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 013 status to ✅. Record any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the grep finds a Compose `mammoth` / `docxToTipTapHtml` call site that is NOT one of the two known branches (`ComposeEditor.tsx:1667`/`:1718`) or `docxToTipTapHtml` in `docxBridge.ts` — i.e. an unexpected consumer — STOP and surface per root CLAUDE.md §6 before deleting. There may be an entry path not covered by 010-012; deleting blind would break it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Renders via projection, no console errors">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a docx in Compose via each entry path (upload, browse, open-in-Compose).</step>
        <step>Confirm the editor renders content and the browser console shows no errors/warnings from the removed reader.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All three paths render via the server projection; no `mammoth`/`docxToTipTapHtml` reference or error in the console.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle the app to dark theme with a docx open in Compose.</step>
        <step>Toggle back to light theme.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The editor surface renders theme-correct in both dark and light (ADR-021); no unstyled/inverted regions from the deletion.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <outputs>
